    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nI have my key mappings grouped by prefixes, and with `mini.clue` I want to make some of the keys \"submodes\".\r\n\r\nMy current config set empty mappings for key group prefixes to give them descriptions:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>d\", \"\", { desc = \"description for the group\" })\r\n```\r\nBut it turns out this doesn't work well with `postkeys`. If I configure it like this:\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  triggers = {\r\n    {mode = \"n\", keys = \"<leader>\"}\r\n  },\r\n  clues = {\r\n    {mode = \"n\", keys = \"<leader>dh\", postkeys = \"<leader>d\"}\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nthe empty `<leader>d` keymap rather than the `<leader>` trigger is activated, so the clue window exits immediately.\r\nShould this be considered a problem with `mini.clue`? Or should I accept it and rewrite my empty mappings for groups to clues instead?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have my key mappings grouped by prefixes, and with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.clue</code> I want to make some of the keys \"submodes\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My current config set empty mappings for key group prefixes to give them descriptions:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;&lt;leader&gt;d&quot;, &quot;&quot;, { desc = &quot;description for the group&quot; })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>description for the group<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But it turns out this doesn't work well with <code class=\"notranslate\">postkeys</code>. If I configure it like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  triggers = {\n    {mode = &quot;n&quot;, keys = &quot;&lt;leader&gt;&quot;}\n  },\n  clues = {\n    {mode = &quot;n&quot;, keys = &quot;&lt;leader&gt;dh&quot;, postkeys = &quot;&lt;leader&gt;d&quot;}\n  }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">{\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">triggers</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    {<span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;leader&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>}\n  },\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">clues</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    {<span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;leader&gt;dh<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">postkeys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>}\n  }\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">the empty <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;leader&gt;d</code> keymap rather than the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;leader&gt;</code> trigger is activated, so the clue window exits immediately.<br>\nShould this be considered a problem with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.clue</code>? Or should I accept it and rewrite my empty mappings for groups to clues instead?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nI have my key mappings grouped by prefixes, and with mini.clue I want to make some of the keys \"submodes\".\nMy current config set empty mappings for key group prefixes to give them descriptions:\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>d\", \"\", { desc = \"description for the group\" })\nBut it turns out this doesn't work well with postkeys. If I configure it like this:\n{\n  triggers = {\n    {mode = \"n\", keys = \"<leader>\"}\n  },\n  clues = {\n    {mode = \"n\", keys = \"<leader>dh\", postkeys = \"<leader>d\"}\n  }\n}\nthe empty <leader>d keymap rather than the <leader> trigger is activated, so the clue window exits immediately.\nShould this be considered a problem with mini.clue? Or should I accept it and rewrite my empty mappings for groups to clues instead?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
