            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Should this be considered a problem with `mini.clue`? Or should I accept it and rewrite my empty mappings for groups to clues instead?\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a problem with 'mini.clue'. Having real mappings for both `<Leader>d`  and `<Leader>dh` is a bit problematic in itself.\r\n\r\nWhat indeed should work is to have real mappings only for the actions you want to do outside of 'mini.clue' and put a group description in `config.clues`. So something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.clue').setup({\r\n  triggers = {\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>' },\r\n  },\r\n  clues = {\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>d', desc = 'Group' },\r\n\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dh', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dj', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dk', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dl', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is more or less documented in [\"Leader clues\"](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-clue.html#miniclue-examples-leaderclues) section together with [submode example](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-clue.html#miniclue-examples-submodes-submodeexamples). Although the latter should probably set up `<Leader>` as a trigger and `<Leader>m` as a group clue.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Should this be considered a problem with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.clue</code>? Or should I accept it and rewrite my empty mappings for groups to clues instead?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't think this is a problem with 'mini.clue'. Having real mappings for both <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Leader&gt;d</code>  and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Leader&gt;dh</code> is a bit problematic in itself.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What indeed should work is to have real mappings only for the actions you want to do outside of 'mini.clue' and put a group description in <code class=\"notranslate\">config.clues</code>. So something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.clue').setup({\n  triggers = {\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '&lt;leader&gt;' },\n  },\n  clues = {\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '&lt;leader&gt;d', desc = 'Group' },\n\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '&lt;leader&gt;dh', postkeys = '&lt;leader&gt;d' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '&lt;leader&gt;dj', postkeys = '&lt;leader&gt;d' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '&lt;leader&gt;dk', postkeys = '&lt;leader&gt;d' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '&lt;leader&gt;dl', postkeys = '&lt;leader&gt;d' },\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.clue<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">triggers</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    { <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  },\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">clues</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    { <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Group<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n\n    { <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;dh<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">postkeys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    { <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;dj<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">postkeys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    { <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;dk<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">postkeys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n    { <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;dl<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">postkeys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;d<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  },\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is more or less documented in <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-clue.html#miniclue-examples-leaderclues\" rel=\"nofollow\">\"Leader clues\"</a> section together with <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-clue.html#miniclue-examples-submodes-submodeexamples\" rel=\"nofollow\">submode example</a>. Although the latter should probably set up <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Leader&gt;</code> as a trigger and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Leader&gt;m</code> as a group clue.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Should this be considered a problem with mini.clue? Or should I accept it and rewrite my empty mappings for groups to clues instead?\n\nI don't think this is a problem with 'mini.clue'. Having real mappings for both <Leader>d  and <Leader>dh is a bit problematic in itself.\nWhat indeed should work is to have real mappings only for the actions you want to do outside of 'mini.clue' and put a group description in config.clues. So something like this:\nrequire('mini.clue').setup({\n  triggers = {\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>' },\n  },\n  clues = {\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>d', desc = 'Group' },\n\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dh', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dj', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dk', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>dl', postkeys = '<leader>d' },\n  },\n})\nThis is more or less documented in \"Leader clues\" section together with submode example. Although the latter should probably set up <Leader> as a trigger and <Leader>m as a group clue.",
